  creatureData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 7bbac08f8eef0274bb97b82eec3c9423, type: 2}
  description:
  - While most insects glow by using forms of bioluminescience, these creatures achieve
    their glow via a flammable waxy substance that coats their abdomen. They use
    their high body heat to burn down suitable objects into ash, from which they
    ingest using their probiscis. Their bodies cannot ignite on their own, and require
    a nearby heat source (often being their home hive) to reignite if they were to
    be extinguished.
